ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:[Grant Radar] OJJDP FY 2026 Opioid Affected Youth Initiative — due
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ojjdp-family-treatment-court-fy26-due-20261116@more-grant-radar
DTSTAMP:20261025T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:[Grant Radar] OJJDP FY 2026 Family Treatment Court Program — due
DESCRIPTION:Four-year federal grants (Cat 1 up to $850K\, Cat 2 up to $750K) for courts and local governments to start or expand family treatment courts that pay for SUD and co-occurring treatment for parents in the child welfare system\, with explicit objectives for opioid and stimulant use disorders. MORE fits as evidence-based OUD/SUD treatment capacity: a county or court can budget MORE clinician training for its treatment providers as a contractor/consultant cost or through a subrecipient provider.\n\nPath: Sub · Priority 2.0\nhttps://www.ojp.gov/funding/docs/ojjdp-2026-172738.pdf
URL:https://www.ojp.gov/funding/docs/ojjdp-2026-172738.pdf
